  "hypothesis": "The current policy over-weights failure_rate and stagnation, causing it to repeatedly select recovery (which has failed twice and stagnated) while ignoring modules with high failure_rate but no attempts yet (rag, tools, prompt). A better meta-exploration policy should penalize stagnation more strongly and reward unattempted modules, while still leveraging last_gain to exploit successful mechanisms like memory. Specifically, replacing the (1-attempted) term with a stronger unattempted bonus and adding a stagnation penalty will redirect exploration toward real defects in rag/tools/prompt.",
